Duplicate-fetch race in our Node cache layer. Save /workspace/usercache.mjs:

const cache = new Map();
export async function getUser(id, fetcher) {
  if (cache.has(id)) return cache.get(id);
  const user = await fetcher(id);
  cache.set(id, user);
  return user;
}
export function clearCache() { cache.clear(); }

The check-then-act around the await means N concurrent callers for the same id all invoke fetcher. Reproduce with node:test first: a fetcher that increments a counter and resolves after new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 20)); fire Promise.all of 10 getUser('42', fetcher) calls; assert the counter is 1 and watch it fail with 10. Then fix by caching the in-flight promise itself, and add: on rejection, delete the cache entry so a later call can retry; test that path too with a fetcher that fails once then succeeds. node --test green, including a test that different ids still fetch independently.

